# Upstream source trees, fetched by repo(1) and git rather than kept here:
# AOSP is ~350 GB across 1084 projects and the kernel another ~4 GB. Neither
# carries local changes worth publishing -- the kernel has one small patch, and
# the AOSP delta lives in patches/ -- so both are pinned by revision instead of
# vendored. See doc/README.md.
/android_17/*
/linux/

# Exception: android_17/device/pcx86/ is OUR device target, not upstream.
#
# Re-including a path under an excluded directory requires un-excluding every
# parent in turn, because git never descends into an excluded directory to look
# for exceptions. Spelling it out level by level, as below, confines the walk to
# android_17/device/ -- it does NOT make git traverse the 1084 upstream projects
# or out/.
!/android_17/device/
/android_17/device/*
!/android_17/device/pcx86/

# ...except the cross-built Mesa libraries, which live inside the device tree
# but are build output: ~20 MB of .so produced by ./build.sh mesa. The recipe
# is in git (tools/build-mesa.sh), the artefacts are not -- the same rule the
# kernel and AOSP trees follow.
/android_17/device/pcx86/pc_x86_64/mesa/

# Android Common Kernel, if cloned as a fallback (see doc/03-kernel.md)
/ack/

# Build artefacts
/logs/
/out/

# Disk images and UEFI vars for the QEMU dev VM (see doc/02-host-setup.md)
*.img
OVMF_*.fd
